Its fields are "name", "age" and "color" (line 1).

Line 10: A new dog needs a value for "age".
    let pup be a new dog with name "Pup".
               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Give it after "with", like "with age ...", or give the field a starting value where a dog is defined (line 1), like "..., starting at ...".

Line 11: A new dog needs a value for "name" and "age".
    let odd be a new dog.
               ^^^^^^^^^
Give it after "with", like "with name ...", or give the field a starting value where a dog is defined (line 1), like "..., starting at ...".

Line 12: This gives "name" a value twice.
    let twice be a new dog with name "A" and age 1 and name "B".
                                                       ^^^^
Give each field one value.

Line 13: The field "name" of a dog is text, but this is a number.
    let wrong be a new dog with name 5 and age "old".
                                     ^

Line 13: The field "age" of a dog is a number, but this is text.
    let wrong be a new dog with name 5 and age "old".
                                               ^^^^^

